  "query_preview": "..So far this afternoon storms were forming in the White \nMountains with cumulus fields developing over the higher terrain \nelsewhere. We will see the storms continue to form and gradually \npush to the west and south during the afternoon and eventually into \ncentral Pima County in the evening hours. The latest WRF guidance is \nnot in agreement on the timeline for when storms would potentially \nimpact the Tucson Metro with the WRF-GFS trending on the later side \nand the WRF-HRRR more on the earlier side. To describe how this \ndifference is manifesting, it looks like the WRF-GFS is picking up \non storm development in Cochise County off the Galiuro, Whetstone, \nDragoon, Rincon, and Catalina Mountains around 3 pm to 5 pm MST \nwhich would send outflows and additional storm development into the \nTucson Metro earlier than the WRF-HRRR that does not have this \ndevelopment and instead relies on outflows from the south of Tucson \nand from storms currently pushing off the White Mountains. \nEssentially, we're looking at a two hour time difference depending \non how storm development trends.\n\nThe environment is ripe with instability according to the latest SPC \nmesoanalysis. As of this writing there is 1500-2500 J/kg of MLCAPE \nand around 20-30 kts of effective bulk layer shear as well as DCAPE \nof 1400-1600 J/kg. Given this environment and the trends of the \nconvective allowing models, I think clustering of storms is on the \ntable along with potentially a few stronger discrete quasi \nsupercellular storms.\n\nTomorrow looks a bit similar to today but turning down the intensity \nof all of the ingredients a little bit and with storms centered more \nover the northern portions of our area including Graham, Greenlee, \nand Pinal counties. There will still be showers and storms over the \nrest of the southeast Arizona, but that's where I am initially \nseeing the best ingredients for stronger outflows setting up.\n\nOtherwise, we look to remain in an active weather pattern into the \nweekend as the upper high center moves toward the Four Corners \nThursday into Friday, then into the Rockies by Saturday afternoon. \nThe Extreme Heat Warning remains in effect through Friday evening, \nand we will be monitoring for continuing heat concerns heading into \nthe weekend.",
